{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he lay with Bilhah.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: he disturbed his father's bed. And so in his father's rebuke it is written (Genesis 49): ״אז חללת יצועי עלה״ — then you defiled my couch, he went up. They censured him only for the act of going up, to tell you that he did not sin in the matter of lying with her but only in the disturbing. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory said: anyone who says Reuben sinned is only mistaken. And because he disturbed his father's bed and Jacob did not lie with Bilhah, Scripture holds it against him as though he had lain with her. And so you find with the sons of Eli (1 Samuel 2): ״אשר ישכבון את הנשים הצובאות פתח אהל מועד״ — who would lie with the women who assembled at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting, and it is written (ibid.): ״ותהי חטאת הנערים גדולה מאד את פני יהוה״ — and the sin of the young men was very great before YHWH, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said: because they would bring their offerings up to Shiloh to purify, and would delay them and detain them outside their homes, Scripture holds it against them as though they had lain with them." "<b>And if you count</b> from ״ויסע ישראל״ until ״שנים עשר״ you will find in it a number of words equal to the numerical value of the Name, the designated one, and perhaps there is in this a hint that Reuben did not sin, for the Holy One, blessed be He, testified concerning him with His name — just as He testified with His name upon the names of the tribes, sealing His name within them: הראובני, השמעוני, and likewise all of them." "<b>And the sage Ramban wrote</b> that the statement ״ויהיו בני יעקב שנים עשר״ — and the sons of Jacob were twelve — is to inform us that he did not beget any after the twelve, for because he disturbed his father's bed, he did so out of fear lest he beget more from Bilhah the concubine; therefore Scripture informed us that he did not beget any thereafter at all. And furthermore Scripture states ״ויהיו בני יעקב י״ב״ — and the sons of Jacob were twelve — for all of them are equal in one rank in one enumeration, and just as they did not sin, so too Reuben did not sin."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {1 "The phrase 'השם המיוחד' (the designated Name) refers to the Tetragrammaton, whose gematria is 26; 'Name' here is HaShem in the sense of the divine name counted by letter-value."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:59.898973740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}